        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(x+\\dfrac{d}{c}\\right)\\left(y-\\dfrac{a}{c}\\right)=-\\dfrac{ad-bc}{c^2}=-\\dfrac{D_f}{c^2}$.\n\nExpand the product and use $(cx+d)y=ax+b$.",
          "worked": "Since $(cx+d)y=ax+b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\left(x+\\frac{d}{c}\\right)\\left(y-\\frac{a}{c}\\right)&=\\frac{(cx+d)y}{c}-\\frac{ax}{c}-\\frac{ad}{c^2}\\\\\n\\left(x+\\frac{d}{c}\\right)\\left(y-\\frac{a}{c}\\right)&=\\frac{ax+b}{c}-\\frac{ax}{c}-\\frac{ad}{c^2}\\\\\n\\left(x+\\frac{d}{c}\\right)\\left(y-\\frac{a}{c}\\right)&=\\frac{bc-ad}{c^2}\\\\\n\\left(x+\\frac{d}{c}\\right)\\left(y-\\frac{a}{c}\\right)&=-\\frac{D_f}{c^2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
